MILLION COLOR!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.180
TURNS!

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.900
<i>I ended up having to destroy the star of Dianna's Ancestors.</i>

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.690
<i>And although it saved the lives of over a hundred thousand people from the Moonrace...</i>

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.710
<i>...It still feels like something inexcusable.</i>

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.820
<i>In addition to that, we don't know where those two people from the Red Team have gone off too...</i>

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.490
<i>Nor do we know if the Willgem is safe.</i>

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.910
<i>Yet, I've finally returned to the moon.</i>

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.090
<b>Sea Battle On The Lunar Surface</b>

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.540
What's this?

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.700
Where are you going?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.500
To the port.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.500
A port?

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.500
There's a lot of moss here. Make sure your Kapool doesn't lose its footing.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.300
I still don't understand... A port? Moss?

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.100
We're here.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.020
We've made it to the moon's canals.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.230
- Is right there okay?
- Yes.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.730
Are you alright?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.320
What's going on?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.700
You okay?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.910
I'm fine.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.700
It smells like the sea...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.710
Oh, forgive me.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.500
The ocean? A canal?

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.130
You've held up very well, considering everything that's happened.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.000
It's nothing.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.300
It truly does give off the smell of salt!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.010
THIS is the moon!?

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.430
A river?

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.810
Well, that's why they usually call us rivermen.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.730
It was dark outside...yet how is it so bright in here?

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:40.110
The Canal and the rest of the city are properly lit in accordance with the time on Earth.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.110
The people of the Moonrace were originally part of earth's populous, after all.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.200
So if you grew up near a sea, why were you unable to swim back there?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.330
I did when I was a kid.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.910
You nearly drowned in the river!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.710
That's because it was my first time swimming in a river on the earth!

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.420
The current was faster than expected and the water levels were uneven.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.420
It caught me by surprise.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.420
What?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.510
It's a whale!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.510
A whale?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.220
We don't have any particularly large ones.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.430
I see...

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.100
Huh!? You... couldn't be Loran, could you!?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.730
Hamet? Is that you, Hamet?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.600
Didn't you go down to Earth?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.020
That I did!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.820
Well, then what are you doing back up here?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.110
Why I'm... well, a lot has happened.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.820
Did you hear the news that a war broke out on Earth!?

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.200
They started a war?

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.830
Then, have you heard anything about Dianna Counter's plans to return the population there?

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.210
Hamet... What are you ...Huh!?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.500
Sister Donna?

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.300
Is that Loran Cehack?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.810
Why do we have to do all the carrying around here!?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.400
It's better than back on earth, when we used to have to steal these things!

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:04.400
This is our complete inventory. We'll also return the soldier we rescued back to you.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.410
Here's their inventory!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:18.330
The leader of a North Ameria fiefdom, Duke Borjarno, has decided to help unite each of our respective territories.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:24.510
I understand what you're saying. However, due to the fact that I am a soldier...

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.510
Paperwork and negotiation aren't my specialty.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.140
In that case, whom should I seek?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.010
You're looking for Agrippa Maintainer.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.510
Agrippa?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.310
Then, I would like to have a meeting with this person.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.940
I shall inform him, but it may be some time before I can grant you an interview.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.310
We didn't come all the way here for sight-seeing!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:44.320
When you just show up unannounced, that leaves us with little time to make such provisions.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.530
Well isn't that funny?

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.820
And you are?

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:54.540
Duke Borjarno's thirteenth daughter, Lady Lily Borjarno.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.000
I'll leave the negotiation plans to you, my lord...

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.840
...however, it is rather discourteous of you to force a lady to wait.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.210
Then you're saying that I'm discourteous?

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:10.010
Back on Earth, a lord would never show any discourtesy towards a noble lady, including making her wait.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.020
You earth women are pretty interesting!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.320
You're suggesting Gym Ghingnham loses to earth's men in terms of courtesy, are you not?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.200
Perhaps. Although I will admit, we've only just met.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.130
Grandma, Grandma... I'm going over to the Yunker's house!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:56.100
- C'mon, be quiet, I can't hear!
- I wanna see...

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.810
I'll meet up with you guys after we're done with the tea!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.100
- Hey!
- Sheesh!
- Don't be so stingy, Hamet...

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.520
I didn't tell them anything.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.610
Forgive me. I don't mean to cause any trouble.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.900
Do you feel relaxed here?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.320
You bet. Those space suits were like wearing suits of armor.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.910
It's been rough.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.200
It's a good thing I was with you, Queen Dianna. That way, I didn't feel completely lost out in space.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:22.000
- I think with your sensibilities, Little Miss Sochie, you'd do fine on your own.
- Sure.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.420
Please, have a seat.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.130
I can't believe this!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.300
You were always such a crybaby, Loran!

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.220
How could someone like yourself possibly wage war in an excavated Mobile Suit!?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.720
Everything that Loran's said is quite true.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.930
Is it that hard to believe?

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.730
But... the news hasn't mentioned anything at all about a war...

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.320
Ah, please forgive us! My younger brother is being rather rude...

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:51.610
Not at all. After I left the moon...

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.910
It appears that they put martial law into effect here.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.040
It must've been Agrippa Maintainer.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.500
That's correct.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.000
Gym Ghingnham's space fleet has been coming and going from the moon quite often as of late...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.420
Is that so?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.840
I believe I can see what's going on now.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.710
Then will you be going to Genganam?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.720
Yes. I can't do anything until I've met with Agrippa myself...

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.930
You people!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.310
Everyone, Have any of you been injured?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.310
Good Lord... What did you think you were doing?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.940
Why'd you knock our door down!?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.730
- Can it really be...
- ...Queen Dianna Soriel?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.730
See? I was right after all!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.530
Cent! I thought I told you not to tell anyone about Queen Dianna!?

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.400
- How could I not?
- You should have found a way!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.030
And who's going to fix our door?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.130
This is Harry. Do you read me?

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.130
I apologize for the low output.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.300
I can hear you.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.100
Most of the Moon's systems have been taken over by Agrippa.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.310
Those involved with him were one who delayed our supplies and sent the Assassins.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.310
Agrippa has betrayed us.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.230
Harry...

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.610
What is it?

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.610
Don't get careless.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.320
I understand. After you've met Agrippa y...

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.410
What's that?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.700
Harry? Harry!?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.710
So this is why you're the Royal Guard's commander? Well done.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.800
Eavesdropping is a pretty bad habit, Midgard.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.300
I don't know what you mean.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.300
Who ordered you to follow me?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.430
Was it Ghingnham?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.300
Or perhaps...

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.730
I don't always have to be following somebody's order.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.310
I understand. There's no place for you with Ghingnham.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.230
You could go back to Gendarme, But you'd prefer to benefit from using Queen Dianna!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:57.110
Even if the rumors suggesting there's two are true, Dianna is still Dianna!

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.540
Lieutenant Yan Shikinen, returning for duty.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.800
I thank you for giving me a second chance to redeem myself,

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.920
General Ghingnham and Lieutenant Sweatson Sutero.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.010
Ahh... I feel heavy...

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.890
Landing on the moon is a rather tiring thing for me.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.720
Well, I heard that the Earth's gravity is six times greater than that of the Moon.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.230
So in comparison, it's much lighter here.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.940
Yes?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.110
Lieutenant!?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.910
How is it? Does it feel light?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.700
It's heavy!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.910
Really now? Heavy, you say?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.920
- There's the Willgem.
- Yeah.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.000
If we inspect the spaceport...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:58.720
It's no use. Due to system maintenance, the service has been shut down.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.220
What's happening?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.720
After Queen Dianna left for earth, quite a bit has changed.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.140
What changes?

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.430
Prices have all gone up.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.020
They shut down all but two television channels!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.810
Alcohol prohibition was put in effect!

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:15.320
So I see. Then they've made a lot of changes...

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.740
Hey now, why are you saying such selfish things?

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.910
I wasn't trying to say that it's Queen Dianna's fault!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.620
Right, the problem is with the planners!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.910
Yeah, right! Now that Her Majesty Dianna has returned, everything should be back to normal soon.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.710
Isn't that right, Queen Dianna?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Right.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.710
There, you see? Queen Dianna said so!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.920
For the sake of all of these people...

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.220
I absolutely must stop Agrippa!

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.140
Loran, we can still reach Genganam, right?

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:46.010
Yes, we could get there using the canal...

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.310
But, if Martial Law is in effect, that could make things difficult...

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.310
Loran, we're rivermen, so we know how to navigate these waters.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.310
We'll get you through it.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.900
Rivermen...

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.480
Something from the Canal...

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.650
That's it! A Whale!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.590
What's supposed to be down here?

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.090
Another city.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.930
So then what was that place we were at?

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.010
It was a fishing village.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.100
The center of the town's beneath the canal.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.400
See you, then! I've gotta deliver something.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.610
Sure. We'll wait for you.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:37.900
See you later!

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.900
So the canal is above us?

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:44.910
Right. That town was built up around the canal.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:49.990
That won't do! Try to walk with your feet firmly on the ground!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.120
I see.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.910
Is that a river?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.210
It's a freshwater river, separate from the canal.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.790
This is great!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.010
Ahh, Welcome, Welcome...

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.300
Try them, they're tasty!

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.720
- Here you go!
- Thanks!

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.020
Here. These are delicious.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.810
Hmm, don't you want to eat them?

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.110
Yes.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.690
They're pretty good... but they taste different...

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.400
Delicious.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.700
- It's an Octopus, right?
- Huh!?

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.830
Hmm? Milady, do you not like Octopus?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.700
But I thought they only stick themselves to people!

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.710
Hey, Loran...

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.120
What do you think you're doing? Come over this way!

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.420
You think this will be enough?

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.800
Let's worry about getting it to the sewing mill, first.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.520
- Hamet!
- Yeah?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.810
The sandwiches are ready!

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:01.900
Here you go, Miss Sochie.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.020
Thank you!

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.400
Did I miss anyone?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.400
What's this?

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.200
It's caviar.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.620
The sandwich...

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.330
Stop!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.000
Will this be enough?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.710
It'll be fine!

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:20.920
Hey, hey, Sochie, are you Loran's wife?
- Huh!?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.500
l thought people on Earth liked to hurry up and get married while young.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.010
No, I'm not!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.300
Pull it up now!

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.520
Okay! Stop!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.310
Somehow... it looks just a little bit awkward...

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.110
It's better if it looks a bit uneven anyway.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.900
I guess you're right.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.320
Will it be alright?

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.910
If it has a chance of keeping us safe, it's worth it.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.410
Her Highness is even willing to do hard labor for us...

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.630
I say painting the Mobile Suit would've been a lot quicker and easier...

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.300
But, then it wouldn't be the White Doll anymore if we painted it black!

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.090
There, there...

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.430
Cent, you've been given a pretty big responsibility, you know?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.720
Yeah, I get it.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.390
If you follow the canal's flow, you'll get to Genganam in about an hour.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:21.020
Additionally, if security passes you in a submarine, they probably won't stop and inspect you either.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.020
Right.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.110
Cent, we'll be counting on you!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.190
I know, I know!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.610
Is something wrong?

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.410
You're our Queen's Knight, so give it your best!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.830
Milady, Let's head out.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:36.990
Roger.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.910
What does that alarm mean?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.000
There are Mobile Suits within the vicinity of the canal...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.630
They're usually just patrolling the region out in orbit.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:02.310
There we are!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.690
Even if they're within the territory of the Canal...

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.030
...this is a very unusual emergency.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.030
But, if we start a battle by the riverside...!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.530
You moron!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.000
If we were able to choose our battlefield, we wouldn't have to work so hard.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.290
Our forces have been training for over 2000 years just for this very day!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.220
They've made it in!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.600
Mobile Suits are here?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.190
Why are the Mahiroo...!?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.530
They're coming back!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.700
Did they find him?

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.910
That infared reading is too large to be a whale!

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.710
How about a light prick, then?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.130
I've been discovered?

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.010
Here comes the wave!

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.220
I'll recover my honor!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.100
Did he succeed?

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.230
No, I can't fire!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.690
What are you doing!?

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.190
You can't do it, Milady!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:35.030
If there's an explosion down here, the river will be wrecked, and the city under it will be flooded as well!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.400
But that city belongs to the enemy...

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.700
...and it was my home town as well!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.410
I don't think we'll make it!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.700
Please, wait a moment...

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.330
What is it?

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.790
Reduce your output.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.210
When they surface, let them taste 100% of our power!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.420
It's no good... Loran will...

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:56.930
Hamet, let's get going!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.090
Can you beat em, Loran!?

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:08.600
Your so called capital of the Moon appears to be a rather lonesome looking place.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.520
That's just on the Lunar Surface...

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.190
But it's designed so that we can live comfortably in towns and by the canals.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:18.030
These canals run through your society like blood vessels, don't they?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.990
Oh? For a Terran, you've certainly done your homework.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:25.500
Well, I needed to study enough in order to carry out negotiations with your Moonrace.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.210
General Ghingnham!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.000
Where have you been?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.500
How did you hurt your arm?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.420
Consider it a bite from an unruly dog.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.920
And also...

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:41.510
It would appear as though my people have discovered some traitors among the Moonrace.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.600
Sweatson has engaged them in mobile suit combat.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.890
Could it be our missing mechanical doll?

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.310
What was that?

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:51.600
If that is so, please consider capturing and returning it to us.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:53.520
You would like it returned, you say?

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:58.030
Since they're deserters, I'd like to reacquire them and personally sentence them to die by a firing squad.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.200
Such is the custom on earth.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.700
I see! That's rather amusing...

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.910
You want to him dead, and yet you're asking us to capture him for you alive!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.710
Please get away from here, Queen Dianna!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.300
Shit...

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:22.590
I had you in my sights...

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.390
Are the rivermen helping him?

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:31.810
If I can disable the generator, I can prevent it from exploding...

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:38.030
If you run away, what sort of opponent are you for me?

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:42.030
But I suppose a person makes do and has fun with what they get.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:46.410
I'm going to use my Cross Crusher, then!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.290
Consider your surroundings!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:54.500
What was that!?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:19:59.800
It failed?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.010
You're a naive one, White Mustache!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.730
Come on!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.520
Loran's battling against the Mahiroo...

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.110
All of you, l know you're scared, but we have to help him!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.700
These are...

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.500
Whales, now!?

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.500
Let's do it!

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.300
Where'd the White Mustache go!?

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:52.020
Mustached bastard!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:59.110
Why is this happening!?

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.990
How in the world could this happen!?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.490
Are you alright, Lieutenant?

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.120
All troops, retreat! Give me some support!

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:20.920
Lieutenant!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.300
We didn't shake the submarine too much, right?

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:28.930
It still shook quite a bit.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:32.220
Truly, thank you for your help, Sister Donna, Hamet!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.390
This made us both very happy, Loran.

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:36.020
Why is that?

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.310
Even after you left for earth, you never forgot the fact that you were once a riverman.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:42.320
You protected our canal from being destroyed even as you fought.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:45.610
It was nothing. That's just the way things ended up happening.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:48.410
Loran, please escort the Queen safely to Genganam.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.700
Right.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:50.990
Where are we heading now?

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.330
Down below.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.500
Cent, please dive to the bottom and let us get a glance.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:03.500
Those lights down there are from the city of Genganam, Miss Sochie.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:06.300
These lights... are the lights from a city?

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:11.010
That's correct. The Moon's capital, Genganam.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:45.230
<i>With Lady Lily's help, the Militia finally arrives for its negotiations with Agrippa Maintainer.</i>

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:47.400
<i>However, the Mahiroo team appears once again.</i>

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:49.400
<i>They demand that we hand over White Doll...</i>

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:52.950
<i>Or else they will kill Queen Dianna and the other guests.</i>

00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:56.410
<i>What in the world has happened to the Moon's capital?</i>

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:02.620
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...<i>
Determined To Fight</i>

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:05.590
"Where did the wind go now?"

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:08.460
<b>Determined To Fight</b>
